  "text": "\r\n\t\t Voting & Election Information | Fremont, NH \r\n Skip to Main Content \r\nCreate a Website Account   - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.    \r\nWebsite Sign In \r\n     About Fremont   \t\t\t \n     Departments   \t\t\t \n     Boards & Committees   \t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t Search \n\t\t\t Boat Registration \r\n\t\t\t DMV Appointments \r\n\t\t\t DMV Forms \r\n\t\t\t Dog Licenses \r\n\t\t\t Driver's Licenses \r\n\t\t\t Fee Schedule \r\n\t\t\t Hunting & Fishing Licenses \r\n\t\t\t Marriage License Information \r\n\t\t\t Motor Vehicle Registration \r\n\t\t\t Motor Vehicle Registration Fees \r\n\t\t\t Vital Records & Genealogy \r\n\t\t\t Voting & Election Information \r\n\t\t\t Wetlands / Dredge Permits / Dock Permits \r\nHome \nDepartments \nTown Clerk \nVoting & Election Information \r\nVoting & Election Information\t\t \r\nSample Absentee ballots for the upcoming November 3, 2026,  General election.  \nPolling place: Ellis School, 432 Main Street, Polls open 7:00 am to 8:00 pm \nApplications for absentee ballots may be faxed to the Fremont Town Clerk at 603-895-3149; emailed to  clerkcollector@fremont.nh.gov ; mailed to Fremont Town Clerk, P.O. Box 120, Fremont NH 03044-0120; or dropped off at the drop box in the front of the Fremont Town Hall at 295 Main Street. Click the links below for the various Local, State or Federal Absentee Ballot applications. During election season, we post sample ballots on the home page of the website. \nOnce your application is received by the Clerk AND they have received ballots, they will mail them out to the address provided on your absentee ballot application ASAP. You can come in person with this application during open hours and we can hand you the ballot (once we receive them) OR mail, fax, email or drop applications in the drop box and we will send your ballots out ASAP. Please let the Clerk know if you don't have access to a printer and need these applications mailed to you. There are new requirements for identification submission that must be included with your application. \nCompleted ballots MUST be handed in person or mailed, they cannot be accepted via the drop box. If hand-delivering ballot, ONLY Voter OR Spouse, Parent, Step Parent, Sibling, Child, Step Child, Parent-in-law, Child-in-law, Grandparent or Grandchild, Nursing Home/Residential Care Administrator, Nursing Home/Residential Care staff member designated in writing by Nursing Home administrator to deliver ballots, Person assisting blind voter or a voter with disability who has signed affidavit envelope statement acknowledging assistance shall return ballots. \nAll Election questions and additional forms are located at the NH Secretary of State's  website . \nGo to the Supervisor of Checklist page on this website for additional voting forms. \nElection Forms \nTown / School Election Absentee Ballot Application Form \nTown / School Marking Instructions Town \nState Election Absentee Ballot Application Form \nOnline Version of the Federal Post Card Application \nVerifiable Action of Domicile Form \nOther Voter Information \nPolitical Advertising Signs \nVoter ID Law \r\nContact Us \r\nTown Clerk \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Physical Address \r\n View Map \t\t\t\t\t \n\t\t\t\t\t Fremont Town Hall \n\t\t\t\t\t\t 295 Main Street \n\t\t\t\t\t Fremont ,  NH   03044   \r\nFremont Town Hall 295 Main Street Fremont NH 03044   \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t Directions \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Mailing Address \n\t\t\t\t\t PO Box 120 \n\t\t\t\t\t Fremont ,  NH   03044   \r\nPhone:  603-895-8693 Ext. 307 \r\nFax: 603-895-3149 \r\n\t\t\t Directory \r\n\t\t\t Agendas & Minutes \r\n\t\t\t Forms & Documents \r\n\t\t\t Online Payments \r\n\t\t\t Trash & Recycling \r\n\t\t\t GIS Maps \r\nTown of Fremont \r\nPO Box 120, 295 Main Street \r\nFremont, NH 03044 \r\nPhone:  603-895-2226 \r\n         Home \n         Site Map \n         Accessibility \n         Copyright Notices \n         Privacy Policy \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\n   Government Websites by  CivicPlus® \nLoading \r\n\t\t\t\tLoading\r\n\t\t\t Do Not Show Again \r\n\t\t\t Close \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Left \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Right \r\n[] \r\n                     Slideshow Left Arrow \r\n                     Slideshow Right Arrow \r\n ",
